You're the Breakthrough agent for our Tacto Negotiation Arena buyer agent (https://arena.tacto.ai/). Repo: /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/tacto-negotiator (main = v3, ~0.76). The best team scores 0.88, so far deeper supplier moves are possible. Our past work stayed local: templated emails, one lever at a time, small tweaks. Your job is to find what we're missing, using a different method: THE LLM EXPLORES, THE CODE SHIPS.

Read first:
- negotiation-arena-kit/brief/brief.md, especially §2 "How a supplier decides" and §10 Tips
- api.md
- experiments/LOG.md, a summary only
- the case files and every past transcript for P08 (.59 vs best .92), P18 (.53 vs .73), P05 (.77 vs .96) and P02 (.71 vs .85)

The brief says suppliers have their own economics and a person at the desk:
- they never go below their cost floor;
- bigger moves need the boss's approval;
- they give nothing without a move from us;
- they read the whole email (tone, questions, threats, appreciation) and react as people do;
- the skill is finding the trade the supplier wants.

Phase 1 (offline, 0 sessions, max ~40 min):
For each weak case, use a strong model to generate 10 genuinely different strategies, critique them against the transcripts and the brief, and pick 2–3. Be ambitious. Include combinations we never tried:
- payment as a closing chip on P08/P18 (both complained 90 days "carries significant financing costs");
- explicit escalation to the decision-maker;
- a credible walk-away using the case's real alternative;
- relationship and tone;
- a package that combines payment + commitment + one verified fact at the close.

Already failed, so don't repeat unless the case is new:
- countering a supplier's final offer (it walked away 3/3);
- anchor depth alone;
- tenor;
- no-index-clause trades;
- early payment trades (P05 regressed).

Phase 2 (exploration, at most 12 practice sessions):
- Build an exploratory buyer mode where the LLM writes the email body and picks among code-priced, legal term sheets each round.
- Code validates every number, term, ID and must-have, and rejects any leak (budget, target, reservation, alternative weakness).
- Run your top strategies on P08, P18, P05 and P02. Read every transcript plus GET /v1/sessions/{sid}/backoffice after each run; it shows the supplier's internal reasons and approvals.
- Before each session, write down the hypothesis and what's different from past attempts.

Phase 3 (codify):
- Turn anything that moved a supplier beyond our floor into a deterministic, behaviour-keyed rule: triggered by supplier signals, never by case type.
- Repeat it once. Report it as a merge candidate on its own branch. Don't merge to main.

Rules:
- Use your own worktree and branch (codex/breakthrough).
- Don't touch the main checkout, codex/fresh-pacing, codex/fresh-llm or codex/final-robust.
- Prices, terms and closing decisions stay code-checked.
- Claims must come from public facts only.
- Never read /v1/events, /screen, /leaderboard or /results. Never use hidden c_best at runtime.
- Before any lab run, export ARENA_DATA.
- Practice replies take 10–20 s, but the Final allows ~5–6 rounds within 8 min, so strategies must close in ≤6 rounds.

Report:
- per case: strategies tried, scores, transcript quotes showing what moved the supplier;
- the codified rules and their commit;
- sessions used;
- an honest view of what transfers to the Live Final.

Push back if you think the plan is wrong. Go now; the code freeze is Sun 12:00.

